# PART 14 — TRANSACTIONS AND CONCURRENCY

Pay special attention to concurrency.

Two admins may attempt to approve the same request.

Two bookings may attempt to reserve the same room.

A timetable may change after a solver proposal is created.

A dataset may be activated while another import is running.

Use:
- Transactions.
- Appropriate row locks.
- Optimistic version checks.
- Unique constraints.
- Idempotency records.
- Atomic state transitions.
- Stale proposal detection.

Never trust a previous availability check as proof that a resource is still free at commit time.

Revalidate inside the transaction before applying a critical decision.

